{"title":"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">2006 AMC 12A #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">2006 AMC 10A #5</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Doug and Dave shared a pizza with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equally-sized slices. Doug wanted a plain pizza, but Dave wanted anchovies on half the pizza. The cost of a plain pizza was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars, and there was an additional cost of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars for putting anchovies on one half. Dave ate all the slices of anchovy pizza and one plain slice. Doug ate the remainder. Each paid for what he had eaten. How many more dollars did Dave pay than Doug?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301500631794bb0cefa0a56159bac89b24d9e7e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 2\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 3\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }  5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dave and Doug paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a677eaa69013089776cc8196d7389fa023b3e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+2=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> dollars in total.  Doug paid for three slices of plain pizza, which cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6739888e5175f90fd598b3b2629fc99734e550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 8=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />.  Dave paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca23217407e3615b4c90fbb9a1fde93d8456e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-3=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> dollars.  Dave paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c9df65de4057dc421e078e5f88aa269d6229225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7-3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"123\" height=\"30\" /> more dollars than Doug.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A\">200